      "level": 1,
      "content": "Loop through questions"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "We use a while loop to run the same steps for each question. Without arrays yet we use a fixed number of questions (e.g. 5) and a counter. Each time through the loop we ask for an answer, validate it, and update the score."
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet_list",
      "items": [
        "start counter at 0",
        "while counter is less than total questions",
        "do one question",
        "add 1 to the counter"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "content": "1var score = 0;\n2var i = 0;\n3var total = 5;\n4var correctAnswer = \"A\";\n5\n6while (i < total) {\n7  var num = i + 1;\n8\n9  console.log(\"Q\" + num + \". Enter A, B, or C:\");\n10  var userAnswer = prompt(\"Your answer: \");\n11\n12  if (userAnswer) {\n13    userAnswer = userAnswer.trim().toUpperCase();\n14  }\n15\n16  if (userAnswer === correctAnswer) {\n17    score++;\n18  }\n19  i++;\n20}\n21\n22console.log(\"Score: \" + score + \"/\" + total);"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here we loop 5 times. Each time we show a question number, prompt for an answer, normalize it, and if it matches the correct answer we add 1 to score."
    },
